WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:04.020
Every guideline rests
on layers of evidence.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:10.490
In juvenile idiopathic arthritis alone,
about two new papers appear every day.

3
00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:15.977
In a classic review, two reviewers
screen every paper by hand,

4
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.757
and a third settles each disagreement.

5
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.930
It is slow exactly where
rigour matters most.

6
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:27.840
In published medicine, about one quotation
in six does not support its claim.

7
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.557
Our last review, done this way,
took eighteen months,

8
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.420
and its trail was hard to audit.

9
00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.300
This time, we asked Julie.

10
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:50.680
Julie keeps the rigour of a systematic
review, and takes on the repetitive work.

11
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.937
Two independent models
screen every record;

12
00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.910
where they disagree,
a person decides.

13
00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:02.400
Every number leads back to its source.

14
00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:07.887
Built to bring it down to months,

15
00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:10.380
even weeks, with every step on record.

16
00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.977
At the consensus meeting,
clinical experience decides.

17
00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:17.720
That part cannot be automated.

18
00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.247
Julie does not run your searches,
decide recommendations,

19
00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.260
or replace expert reading.

20
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.814
A general assistant answers.

21
00:01:26.897 --> 00:01:29.907
Julie follows the structure
of a systematic review,

22
00:01:29.990 --> 00:01:32.170
and keeps a full audit trail.

23
00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.797
When a colleague asks
where a number comes from,

24
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.510
the answer is one line away.

25
00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:45.670
In our own checks, trained reviewers
made the same mistake as the model.

26
00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:51.410
A language model used without method
is a trial run without randomisation.

27
00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:54.607
Neither is enough on its own.

28
00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:56.710
It takes a planned system.

29
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.510
Behind every line, a patient.
